  "known_limitation": {
    "finding": "D3Q19 staircase moving wall (naive Ladd) drives a spurious m=2 flow",
    "detail": "In the 3D annulus the naive Ladd moving-wall correction injects mass at the axis-crossing corner nodes of the staircase circle (node-wise m=2 pattern, net injection zero). Implemented a mass-conserving variant (subtract the per-node weighted mean of c_k.u_w) which removes the mass drift (2.6e-2 -> 1.7e-13) but not the spurious momentum slip: the profile error stays ~14 % (interior) / 63 % (nominal) versus 2 % for the verified D2Q9 annulus at the same parameters.",
    "measured": {
      "d3q19_naive_mass_drift": 0.0259,
      "d3q19_mass_conserving_mass_drift": 1.71e-13,
      "d3q19_mass_conserving_profile_nominal": 0.5941,
      "d3q19_mass_conserving_profile_interior": 0.138,
      "d2q9_profile_nominal_same_params": 0.0112
    },
    "consequence": "the Taylor-Couette anchor of this node uses the verified D2Q9 annulus (RotatingAnnulusD2Q9) instead of the D3Q19 kernel; the D3Q19 kernel is used only where the walls are lattice aligned (plane channel) or where there are no moving walls (duct)",
    "d2q9_annulus_mass_drift": 0.0051650387193888205,
    "d2q9_note": "the verified D2Q9 annulus keeps the classical staircase moving-wall mass injection (drift ~2e-3 at a 2 % profile error): harmless there, destructive in D3Q19 (2.6e-2).  Reported, not hidden; the profile/torque anchors are unaffected."
  },
